IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bca-gambler`
IMPORT `bca-qa`

-- Betting Control Act 1954 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (bca-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question with a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the situation FALSE and every later input ASSUMEd.
-- For the gambler (the baseline's seat), each question is also asked against the baseline export on the same facts.
-- Mirror cases ask the same facts from the gambler and the bookmaker (s 21(1), s 32(2), (3)). Expected values are worked
-- by hand from the deposited text, never copied from the output. Jake (39) and Ruby (12) are the baseline's people; the
-- others are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked bet` IS A `My bet`
ASSUME `an unasked thing` IS A `Something I might do`

`as the gambler` MEANS `I bet, or want to bet, on races or other events`
`as the bookmaker` MEANS `I am a bookmaker licensed under the Act, or a bookmaker's licensed manager or employee`

-- A bet made online, at fixed odds, on an event permitted by another State's law and not prohibited, not known to be with
-- an unauthorised operator; the rest as given.
GIVEN `operator` IS A `Who I bet with`, `age` IS A NUMBER, `in WA` IS A BOOLEAN, `event outside WA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knows not authorised` IS A BOOLEAN, `as the Act allows` IS A BOOLEAN, `social` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My bet`
`a bet with` MEANS `My bet` WITH
    `who I bet with` IS `operator`
    `my age in years` IS `age`
    `I am in WA when I make it` IS `in WA`
    `I make it by telephone or online` IS TRUE
    `it is a fixed odds bet` IS TRUE
    `the event is outside WA` IS `event outside WA`
    `the Commission has approved bookmaking on the event under s 4B` IS FALSE
    `betting on the event is permitted by the law of another State or Territory` IS TRUE
    `the event is a prescribed prohibited event or contingency` IS FALSE
    `I know, or would be expected to know, the operator is not authorised` IS `knows not authorised`
    `the bookmaker takes it as the Act allows` IS `as the Act allows`
    `it is social gambling or permitted gaming under the Gaming and Wagering Commission Act 1987` IS `social`

`Jake on the TAB app, Ascot` MEANS `a bet with` `the TAB run by RWWA` 39 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`Ruby on the TAB app` MEANS `a bet with` `the TAB run by RWWA` 12 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` MEANS `a bet with` `an operator licensed in another State or Territory` 39 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`Jake on an unexempted offshore site he knows of` MEANS `a bet with` `an offshore operator the Commission has not exempted` 39 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`Jake on the TAB app, in Bali` MEANS `a bet with` `the TAB run by RWWA` 39 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`Jake with an SP bookie` MEANS `a bet with` `an unlicensed bookmaker` 39 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`Jake in the office tipping` MEANS `a bet with` `a friend or workmate, privately` 39 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`Jake in a private card game for money` MEANS `a bet with` `a friend or workmate, privately` 39 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`Jake with an on-course bookmaker` MEANS `a bet with` `a bookmaker licensed under this Act` 39 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`Jake with a bookmaker off the rails` MEANS `a bet with` `a bookmaker licensed under this Act` 39 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `For the gambler`

-- s 27A(1): an NT app on an AFL match in Melbourne is an interstate bet; the TAB on Ascot is not.
#ASSERT `Is my bet an interstate or offshore bet under the Act` `as the gambler` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my bet an interstate or offshore bet under the Act` `as the gambler` `Jake on the TAB app, Ascot` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my bet an interstate or offshore bet under the Act` `as the gambler` `Jake on the TAB app, Ascot` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my bet an interstate or offshore bet` `Jake on the TAB app, Ascot`)
-- s 27A(1) "authorised person": an operator licensed in another State is; RWWA is not on the list; an unexempted
-- offshore operator is not.
#ASSERT `Is the operator I bet with an authorised person` `as the gambler` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is the operator I bet with an authorised person` `as the gambler` `Jake on the TAB app, Ascot` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the operator I bet with an authorised person` `as the gambler` `Jake on an unexempted offshore site he knows of` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the operator I bet with an authorised person` `as the gambler` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is the operator an authorised person` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne`)
-- s 27A(1) "permitted event": permitted by another State's law and not prohibited.
#ASSERT `Is the event I bet on a permitted event` `as the gambler` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is the event I bet on a permitted event` `as the gambler` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is it a permitted event` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne`)
-- s 27A(2): an offshore bet with an operator he knows is not authorised: an offence; the NT app: not.
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 27A by this bet` `as the gambler` `Jake on an unexempted offshore site he knows of` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 27A by this bet` `as the gambler` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 27A by this bet` `as the gambler` `Jake on an unexempted offshore site he knows of` EQUALS `yes if` (`Do I commit an offence under s 27A` `Jake on an unexempted offshore site he knows of`)
-- ss 22-24, 27A: the TAB at 39 lawful; at 12 an offence ($2 000, s 22(2)); the NT app uncertain ($100 000 on the literal
-- reading); offshore known unauthorised an offence ($10 000); from Bali outside the Act ($0); an SP bookie an offence
-- ($100 000, s 24(1)(b)); office tipping as social gambling lawful; a private game that is not, an offence ($100 000,
-- s 23(1)); an on-course bookmaker as the Act allows lawful; off the rails an offence ($100 000, s 24(1)(c)).
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake on the TAB app, Ascot` EQUALS `lawful: the Act allows it`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Ruby on the TAB app` EQUALS `an offence by you`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` EQUALS `uncertain: ss 23(1) or 24(1)(b) read literally reach it, though the Act licenses or tolerates it elsewhere`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake on an unexempted offshore site he knows of` EQUALS `an offence by you`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake on the TAB app, in Bali` EQUALS `outside the Act: you are not in WA`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake with an SP bookie` EQUALS `an offence by you`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake in the office tipping` EQUALS `lawful: the Act allows it`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake in a private card game for money` EQUALS `an offence by you`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake with an on-course bookmaker` EQUALS `lawful: the Act allows it`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake with a bookmaker off the rails` EQUALS `an offence by you`
#ASSERT `What does the Act make of this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` EQUALS `the answer for` (`What does the Act make of my bet` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne`)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake on the TAB app, Ascot` EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Ruby on the TAB app` EQUALS amount 2000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake on an NT app, AFL in Melbourne` EQUALS amount 100000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake on an unexempted offshore site he knows of` EQUALS amount 10000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake on the TAB app, in Bali` EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake with an SP bookie` EQUALS amount 100000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake in a private card game for money` EQUALS amount 100000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Jake with a bookmaker off the rails` EQUALS amount 100000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for this bet of mine` `as the gambler` `Ruby on the TAB app` EQUALS amount (`What is the most I can be fined for this bet` `Ruby on the TAB app`)
-- ss 23(2), 26, 21(2)(c) with s 30(1)(b): $20 000, $2 000, $5 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for doing this` `as the gambler` `place a bet for, or help someone bet with a bookmaker who is under a s 25 court order (s 23(2))` EQUALS amount 20000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for doing this` `as the gambler` `not move on when police suspect I am loitering to bet (s 26)` EQUALS amount 2000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for doing this` `as the gambler` `take liquor into a place where a totalisator is operating (s 21(2)(c))` EQUALS amount 5000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for doing this` `as the gambler` `keep watch for police for unlawful betting (s 26B)` EQUALS amount (`What is the most I can be fined for` `keep watch for police for unlawful betting (s 26B)`)
-- s 28(2): convicted, and the money proved to be from the betting: forfeited; not proved: no.
#ASSERT `Must my money from unlawful betting be forfeited` `as the gambler` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must my money from unlawful betting be forfeited` `as the gambler` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must my money from unlawful betting be forfeited` `as the gambler` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Must my betting money be forfeited` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 21(1), (3): not if I appear under 18 or drunk.
#ASSERT `May a WA bookmaker or the TAB knowingly take my bet` `as the gambler` FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May a WA bookmaker or the TAB knowingly take my bet` `as the gambler` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May a WA bookmaker or the TAB knowingly take my bet` `as the gambler` FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May a WA bookmaker or the TAB knowingly take my bet` `as the gambler` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`May a bookmaker or the TAB take my bet` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `May the wagering licensee give me credit for a bet` `as the gambler` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May the wagering licensee give me credit for a bet` `as the gambler` EQUALS `yes if` `May the wagering licensee give me credit`
-- s 25: the Court satisfied: yes; up to 1 year; the Act does not say who applies.
#ASSERT `Can the Magistrates Court order that no bookmaker bet with me` `as the gambler` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Magistrates Court order that no bookmaker bet with me` `as the gambler` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Magistrates Court order that no bookmaker bet with me` `as the gambler` FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can the Court order that no bookmaker bet with me` FALSE)
#ASSERT `For how long at most can a s 25 order on me last` `as the gambler` EQUALS `up to` 1
#ASSERT `For how long at most can a s 25 order on me last` `as the gambler` EQUALS `up to` `For how many years at most can the order last`
#ASSERT `Does the Act say who may ask for a s 25 order` `as the gambler` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the Act say who may ask for a s 25 order` `as the gambler` EQUALS `yes if` `Does the Act say who may apply for the order`
-- s 25(2): renewed if the Court thinks I have not reformed; s 25(3): no offence by me.
#ASSERT `Can the s 25 order on me be renewed` `as the gambler` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the s 25 order on me be renewed` `as the gambler` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the s 25 order on me be renewed` `as the gambler` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can the order on me be renewed` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by betting while the s 25 order is on me` `as the gambler` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by betting while the s 25 order is on me` `as the gambler` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` `Do I commit an offence by betting while under the order`
-- s 32(2): 3 days at Ascot (metropolitan), 7 at Kalgoorlie; s 32(3): $500 claimed, $200 disputed: $300 now; $600
-- disputed: nothing now.
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I appeal to the Commission` `as the gambler` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `within` 3
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I appeal to the Commission` `as the gambler` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `within` 7
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I appeal to the Commission` `as the gambler` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `within` (`Within how many days must I appeal` FALSE)
#ASSERT `How much of the part-disputed bet must the bookmaker pay me now` `as the gambler` TRUE 500 200 EQUALS amount 300
#ASSERT `How much of the part-disputed bet must the bookmaker pay me now` `as the gambler` TRUE 500 600 EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `How much of the part-disputed bet must the bookmaker pay me now` `as the gambler` TRUE 500 200 EQUALS amount (`How much must the bookmaker pay me now` 500 200)

§§ `For the bookmaker`

-- s 12: with a permit, in the ring, on a race day, a steward present: yes; no steward but a telephone bet under the
-- regulations: yes; neither: no; no permit: no; outside the ring: no; another day not approved: no.
#ASSERT `May I take bets on this racecourse here and now` `as the bookmaker` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I take bets on this racecourse here and now` `as the bookmaker` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I take bets on this racecourse here and now` `as the bookmaker` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I take bets on this racecourse here and now` `as the bookmaker` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I take bets on this racecourse here and now` `as the bookmaker` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I take bets on this racecourse here and now` `as the bookmaker` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
-- Mirror of the gambler's s 21 cases: same facts, same answers.
#ASSERT `May I knowingly bet with this person` `as the bookmaker` FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I knowingly bet with this person` `as the bookmaker` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I knowingly bet with this person` `as the bookmaker` FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for betting with a person apparently under 18 or drunk` `as the bookmaker` EQUALS amount 5000
-- s 25(3): after notice, not with the person named ($20 000); anyone else is not stopped by the order.
#ASSERT `Does a s 25 order stop me betting with this person` `as the bookmaker` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does a s 25 order stop me betting with this person` `as the bookmaker` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for betting with a person named in a s 25 order` `as the bookmaker` TRUE EQUALS amount 20000
-- Mirror of the gambler's s 32 cases.
#ASSERT `Within how many days may a party appeal to the Commission` `as the bookmaker` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `within` 3
#ASSERT `Within how many days may a party appeal to the Commission` `as the bookmaker` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `within` 7
#ASSERT `How much of the part-disputed bet must I pay now` `as the bookmaker` TRUE 500 200 EQUALS amount 300
#ASSERT `How much of the part-disputed bet must I pay now` `as the bookmaker` TRUE 500 600 EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `Must I give a written acknowledgment of the disputed bet` `as the bookmaker` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I give a written acknowledgment of the disputed bet` `as the bookmaker` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no

§§ `Does not arise`

-- Each question for the roles it is not about: every other input ASSUMEd.
